# Coding Standards

- Max nesting depth: 3. Prefer early returns / guard clauses over nested `if`.
- Max function length: ~60 lines. Extract helpers before growing further.
- Never copy-paste a helper. Put shared logic in `utils/` (Python) or `static/js/eq_core.js` (JS) and import it.
- One concern per function. Route handlers and UI renderers stay thin and delegate.
- Do not nest `def` / `function` inside another function unless it is a trivial one-liner callback.
- Prefer flat data transforms (map/filter) over nested loops with side effects.
- When touching a file that already violates these rules, leave it no worse — extract or flatten what you touch.
